WEBVTT

00:00:08.520 --> 00:00:10.150
Hey, Natsumi.

00:00:11.110 --> 00:00:12.610
What's up, Mom?

00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:14.530
Come here for a minute.

00:00:16.240 --> 00:00:18.080
Hey! Why are you running away?!

00:00:21.080 --> 00:00:24.540
Oh, you're not mad? I thought...

00:00:24.540 --> 00:00:26.420
You thought what?

00:00:26.420 --> 00:00:28.500
You haven't made trouble again, have you?

00:00:28.500 --> 00:00:29.840
No, I didn't.

00:00:30.210 --> 00:00:31.420
So what is it?

00:00:32.340 --> 00:00:35.800
This pond seems so lonely 
without anything living in it.

00:00:36.090 --> 00:00:38.300
Would you go catch something for me?

00:00:38.760 --> 00:00:40.180
You like that kind of thing, don't you?

00:00:40.180 --> 00:00:43.270
I'm not in the mood right now, though...

00:00:43.270 --> 00:00:44.890
I'll pay you.

00:00:44.890 --> 00:00:46.060
All right!

00:00:46.060 --> 00:00:48.480
So, Mommy, how much will you give me?

00:00:48.480 --> 00:00:49.900
I want 1,000 yen.

00:00:49.900 --> 00:00:52.400
I'd like Yukichi-san even more, though.

00:00:52.400 --> 00:00:54.780
You're not getting 1,000. Try 500.

00:00:55.030 --> 00:00:57.450
All right! I'll go invite the 
others and be back later!

00:00:57.450 --> 00:00:58.950
Hang on a minute.

00:00:59.660 --> 00:01:01.740
I'll let you borrow this watch.

00:01:01.740 --> 00:01:03.450
Be back home by curfew.

00:01:03.660 --> 00:01:05.040
Okay!

00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:39.470
<b>Episode 9</b>

00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:39.470
<b>We Looked at the Moon Together</b>

00:02:39.680 --> 00:02:40.970
So then...

00:02:41.260 --> 00:02:45.680
We're going to hold our exciting first 
fishing tournament at this lake!

00:02:45.680 --> 00:02:48.930
Have a great time, everyone!

00:02:49.430 --> 00:02:51.690
Konomi-san, she invited you, too?

00:02:51.690 --> 00:02:54.820
Yeah, out of the blue. 
What's this about, though?

00:02:54.820 --> 00:02:56.360
I'm not sure.

00:02:56.360 --> 00:02:58.150
Natsumi just came out of nowhere saying

00:02:58.150 --> 00:03:00.490
we were going fishing because 
she wanted the money.

00:03:00.650 --> 00:03:03.660
Hey, don't make me sound bad.

00:03:03.660 --> 00:03:06.620
Fishing is more fun with everyone, right?

00:03:06.620 --> 00:03:08.000
I guess it's fine.

00:03:10.000 --> 00:03:12.750
Doing this stuff like the old 
days might not be so bad.

00:03:13.080 --> 00:03:15.840
Do you like fishing, Konomi-san?

00:03:15.840 --> 00:03:17.590
Not so much,

00:03:17.590 --> 00:03:20.590
but I used to fish with Kaede-chan 
and Hikage-chan on occasion.

00:03:20.590 --> 00:03:22.260
Nattsun, what are you going to catch?

00:03:22.260 --> 00:03:24.550
I want to catch a medetai.

00:03:24.550 --> 00:03:27.220
This is a lake. I don't 
think it has sea bream.

00:03:27.560 --> 00:03:28.350
No way...

00:03:28.350 --> 00:03:29.560
You're way too shocked.

00:03:29.930 --> 00:03:31.730
No sea bream, huh?

00:03:32.100 --> 00:03:34.270
I wanted to catch one...

00:03:34.270 --> 00:03:37.230
You say the most outlandish 
things sometimes, Ren-chon.

00:03:38.440 --> 00:03:41.990
But if I find a shell, 
would that be "megadekai?"

00:03:38.550 --> 00:03:38.900
<b>Mede</b>

00:03:38.900 --> 00:03:39.280
<b>Mede +</b>

00:03:39.280 --> 00:03:44.030
<b>Mede + Kai</b>

00:03:40.020 --> 00:03:44.030
<b>Medekai</b>

00:03:41.990 --> 00:03:44.030
Why would you want
it to mean that?

00:03:46.410 --> 00:03:48.410
Whoa, I think I've got a fish!

00:03:48.410 --> 00:03:50.120
Wh-Wh-What do I do?!

00:03:50.120 --> 00:03:52.330
Hurry and pull it up before it runs!

00:03:58.300 --> 00:03:59.170
Ow!

00:03:59.340 --> 00:04:01.010
A-Are you okay?!

00:04:01.010 --> 00:04:02.880
Y-Yeah...

00:04:02.880 --> 00:04:03.800
Huh?

00:04:04.590 --> 00:04:06.050
Where's the fish?

00:04:06.050 --> 00:04:07.800
It's not there?

00:04:07.800 --> 00:04:09.010
I don't see it...

00:04:09.470 --> 00:04:11.560
Maybe it fell back in the lake.

00:04:14.270 --> 00:04:17.940
I'll feel bad if it landed on the 
ground, so I'll go look for it.

00:04:17.940 --> 00:04:18.940
Okay.

00:04:18.940 --> 00:04:21.530
Hey, where'd you go?

00:04:22.490 --> 00:04:24.200
Oh! I got one, too!

00:04:28.580 --> 00:04:29.870
I've got one, too!

00:04:30.240 --> 00:04:31.870
It's a big one!

00:04:33.830 --> 00:04:36.000
Where'd the fish go?

00:04:36.000 --> 00:04:38.710
My fish disappeared, too...

00:04:38.710 --> 00:04:39.840
Huh?

00:04:39.840 --> 00:04:41.590
I can't find it.

00:04:47.390 --> 00:04:50.760
They have no idea how to 
get the timing right.

00:04:50.760 --> 00:04:53.140
Nattsun, I got a bunch of shells.

00:04:53.430 --> 00:04:55.940
You better hurry up and catch a fish, too.

00:04:59.400 --> 00:05:02.190
I wonder if this lake just 
doesn't have any big fish...

00:05:02.610 --> 00:05:05.030
Maybe we should use bread instead of lures.

00:05:05.030 --> 00:05:07.360
Aren't lures fake?

00:05:07.360 --> 00:05:09.450
Why would fish come to eat something fake?

00:05:09.870 --> 00:05:12.040
They're shaped like the fish's prey.

00:05:12.040 --> 00:05:14.200
Some of them smell like prey, too,

00:05:14.200 --> 00:05:17.170
so I guess they look pretty tasty to fish.

00:05:18.540 --> 00:05:23.260
Is that the same theory as why Nee-nee 
was chewing on scented erasers?

00:05:23.260 --> 00:05:25.920
Isn't our teacher too old to 
be doing stuff like that?!

00:05:25.920 --> 00:05:28.840
You never chew on them, Nattsun?

00:05:28.840 --> 00:05:29.850
I got a bite!

00:05:29.850 --> 00:05:31.510
You bite erasers, too?!

00:05:31.510 --> 00:05:32.350
Not me!

00:05:36.100 --> 00:05:38.650
N-Nattsun, you got a fish?!

00:05:38.650 --> 00:05:40.900
It might be... the boss of the lake...

00:05:40.900 --> 00:05:43.650
Natsumi, what are you 
doing? Sitting on air?

00:05:43.650 --> 00:05:46.820
No! It's huge! I've got something huge!

00:05:46.820 --> 00:05:48.780
Ren-chon, go get somebody to help me!

00:05:48.780 --> 00:05:50.200
Got it!

00:05:50.200 --> 00:05:54.200
And it might be too big for the bucket, 
so get something to put it in!

00:05:55.160 --> 00:05:55.540
<b>Mede</b>

00:05:55.540 --> 00:05:55.870
<b>Mede +</b>

00:05:55.870 --> 00:05:57.660
<b>(Nashi)
Mede + Wakaranai</b>

00:05:56.660 --> 00:05:57.660
<b>Mede</b>

00:05:57.750 --> 00:05:58.870
<b>Mede x Help</b>

00:05:59.170 --> 00:06:02.040
Mayday? Is this mayday?!

00:06:02.040 --> 00:06:03.340
Enough of that!

00:06:07.590 --> 00:06:10.220
Oh, Hikage's coming home?

00:06:10.220 --> 00:06:12.850
Yeah, to visit family graves for Ohigan.

00:06:12.850 --> 00:06:15.060
Candy Store! Nee-nee!

00:06:15.060 --> 00:06:17.600
You were here at the perfect time!

00:06:18.140 --> 00:06:20.900
What brings you out here, Renge?

00:06:21.480 --> 00:06:23.730
We were fishing and got a big one!

00:06:23.730 --> 00:06:26.150
Nattsun said it's the boss of the lake!

00:06:26.150 --> 00:06:29.110
Sushi? I'll have pressed mackerel.

00:06:29.110 --> 00:06:31.320
What are you talking about, Nee-nee?

00:06:31.320 --> 00:06:32.820
She said nushi, not sushi.

00:06:32.820 --> 00:06:35.120
She said it wouldn't fit in the bucket!

00:06:35.120 --> 00:06:37.250
I have to take something to put it in!

00:06:37.250 --> 00:06:40.500
Oh, in that case, there's a 
stack of plastic bins in back.

00:06:41.250 --> 00:06:44.920
Heave-ho! Heave-ho!

00:06:42.460 --> 00:06:45.250
Nattsun, I brought help!

00:06:45.250 --> 00:06:46.380
Nice job, Ren-chon!

00:06:46.760 --> 00:06:49.130
Looks like it's bigger than I was expecting.

00:06:49.130 --> 00:06:53.180
We've been fighting it for 
ages, but it's really tough!

00:06:53.180 --> 00:06:54.550
Give me the pole.

00:06:54.550 --> 00:06:56.470
You don't have a fishing net?

00:06:56.470 --> 00:06:58.930
The little bug nets we have 
aren't big enough for this.

00:06:58.930 --> 00:07:00.310
You don't have a net?

00:07:00.310 --> 00:07:03.650
At this size, the line'll snap as 
soon as you get it out of the water.

00:07:03.940 --> 00:07:06.190
Well, what can I do about it?

00:07:08.190 --> 00:07:09.280
Wait, that's it!

00:07:33.180 --> 00:07:35.510
I caught the boss!

00:07:42.140 --> 00:07:43.940
I'm home!

00:07:43.940 --> 00:07:47.730
Mom, look! I caught a carp!

00:07:50.070 --> 00:07:51.400
Uh...

00:07:51.650 --> 00:07:54.360
Sorry you all had to go along with her.

00:07:54.360 --> 00:07:56.160
Oh, it's no problem.

00:07:56.160 --> 00:07:59.120
We'll just go release it into the pond.

00:07:59.120 --> 00:08:00.790
Thank you.

00:08:00.790 --> 00:08:01.910
Hey, Natsumi.

00:08:02.910 --> 00:08:04.370
Oh, yeah! My money!

00:08:04.370 --> 00:08:07.170
Well? It's huge, right? Bring on the praise!

00:08:07.170 --> 00:08:09.000
Isn't it a bit too large?

00:08:09.000 --> 00:08:10.510
And aren't you a bit wet?

00:08:10.510 --> 00:08:13.510
Oh, the net was too small,

00:08:13.510 --> 00:08:15.970
so I dove into the lake to catch the fish.

00:08:15.970 --> 00:08:17.180
Awesome, huh?

00:08:17.180 --> 00:08:18.930
What happened to my watch?

00:08:19.310 --> 00:08:20.520
Watch...?

00:08:23.480 --> 00:08:25.350
I forgot I had it on.

00:08:25.350 --> 00:08:27.610
It broke, but praise me some more!

00:08:28.650 --> 00:08:31.030
You know it's dangerous to dive in the lake!

00:08:31.030 --> 00:08:32.490
And you broke my watch!

00:08:32.650 --> 00:08:34.320
Come here!

00:08:34.320 --> 00:08:38.120
Mayday! Mayday! Mayday!

00:08:42.450 --> 00:08:44.410
It really is big.

00:08:44.410 --> 00:08:46.500
Looks like it'll be hard to care for.

00:08:46.500 --> 00:08:48.880
I want to give it a name.

00:08:52.590 --> 00:08:54.470
Hikarimono Boss!

00:08:57.680 --> 00:08:59.760
Wash up properly.

00:08:59.760 --> 00:09:01.220
Okay...

00:09:05.730 --> 00:09:10.980
Jeez, Nacchan's in seventh grade now, 
and she's still nothing like a girl.

00:09:10.980 --> 00:09:14.320
I don't think age has anything 
to do with it in her case.

00:09:14.990 --> 00:09:17.950
That's it! I've got a great idea!

00:09:22.620 --> 00:09:23.790
What's that?

00:09:23.790 --> 00:09:26.540
Some outfits I wore in middle school.

00:09:26.540 --> 00:09:29.630
Konomi-chan went all the way back home 
to get them and bring them over.

00:09:29.630 --> 00:09:32.630
We're gonna use these to 
make you more like a girl.

00:09:32.920 --> 00:09:35.510
What? I don't need to do that.

00:09:37.010 --> 00:09:39.970
Shouldn't you do stuff 
like that with Nee-chan?

00:09:39.970 --> 00:09:43.220
They are cute outfits... 
I wouldn't mind trying them on.

00:09:43.810 --> 00:09:48.560
I don't have any elementary school outfits 
left that might fit you, though.

00:09:49.480 --> 00:09:51.270
Come on over here, Nacchan.

00:09:53.190 --> 00:09:56.190
Okay, first, let's tame that messy hair.

00:09:56.190 --> 00:09:58.240
What? You're doing my hair, too?

00:09:58.240 --> 00:10:01.950
Of course. Feminine charm 
starts with the hair.

00:10:02.160 --> 00:10:04.200
Komari-chan, got a hair dryer?

00:10:04.200 --> 00:10:05.790
In the changing room.

00:10:05.790 --> 00:10:08.920
Okay, let's take the clothes 
and get you changed, too.

00:10:08.920 --> 00:10:10.330
There's a mirror in there.

00:10:10.330 --> 00:10:13.250
What? There's no need for all that.

00:10:13.250 --> 00:10:15.460
Now, stop. Just do as I say.

00:10:17.800 --> 00:10:18.970
There!

00:10:18.970 --> 00:10:20.970
All done!

00:10:24.850 --> 00:10:26.470
What do you think, Nacchan?

00:10:28.140 --> 00:10:29.560
That's me...

00:10:35.280 --> 00:10:36.690
And that's me...

00:10:36.690 --> 00:10:38.900
Don't make weird poses.

00:10:38.900 --> 00:10:42.030
These clothes seem kinda 
hard to move around in.

00:10:42.030 --> 00:10:43.620
And I don't need all these layers.

00:10:43.620 --> 00:10:46.330
But it's cute. You look like a classy lady.

00:10:46.330 --> 00:10:48.200
You think so, too, right, Komari-chan?

00:10:48.200 --> 00:10:50.620
Huh? Uh...

00:10:51.040 --> 00:10:54.750
Well, it is cute, but I don't know...

00:10:55.500 --> 00:10:56.760
What's this?

00:10:56.760 --> 00:11:00.090
Nee-chan, are you upset that 
I'm the one getting dressed up?

00:11:00.090 --> 00:11:01.510
H-Huh?

00:11:01.510 --> 00:11:03.890
I am not! Why would you think...

00:11:04.550 --> 00:11:08.060
I'll give you my hand-me-downs from 
elementary school, so cheer up.

00:11:08.060 --> 00:11:10.310
Could you try not to say things 
that make me feel worse?!

00:11:10.520 --> 00:11:14.270
Well, it is pretty nice to be called cute.

00:11:14.270 --> 00:11:15.900
Maybe dressing up isn't so bad.

00:11:15.900 --> 00:11:17.570
Oh? Getting into it now?

00:11:17.570 --> 00:11:19.530
I improve through praise.

00:11:19.530 --> 00:11:22.820
I didn't want to praise you because 
I knew you'd let it go to your head.

00:11:23.200 --> 00:11:25.660
So, I've changed. Is this enough?

00:11:25.660 --> 00:11:26.910
Since we've come this far,

00:11:26.910 --> 00:11:28.830
we should get you to behave 
more like a girl, too.

00:11:28.830 --> 00:11:31.580
I don't know anything 
about girly behavior...

00:11:31.580 --> 00:11:33.500
Nacchan, stop.

00:11:33.500 --> 00:11:35.290
Huh? Wh-What?

00:11:35.290 --> 00:11:38.250
Don't sit cross-legged. Sit on your knees.

00:11:38.250 --> 00:11:40.720
What? But my feet will go numb.

00:11:41.510 --> 00:11:44.220
How do you usually sit, Nee-chan?

00:11:44.220 --> 00:11:45.180
The sumo crouch?

00:11:45.180 --> 00:11:46.300
What the heck?

00:11:46.600 --> 00:11:49.470
I usually just sit like a girl.

00:11:49.470 --> 00:11:52.140
I'm not really good at sitting 
like that, either...

00:11:52.140 --> 00:11:53.810
Nacchan, stop.

00:11:53.810 --> 00:11:55.520
What? Did I do something?

00:11:55.520 --> 00:11:57.520
Don't scratch your head.

00:11:57.520 --> 00:12:00.030
Also, you're talking like a boy.

00:12:01.320 --> 00:12:04.200
I have to fix the way I talk, too?

00:12:04.200 --> 00:12:05.700
Of course!

00:12:05.700 --> 00:12:10.250
Man, I really just don't 
think I can be girly.

00:12:10.700 --> 00:12:12.250
You gave up?

00:12:12.960 --> 00:12:14.920
What are you guys doing?

00:12:19.000 --> 00:12:20.840
There's someone here I don't know!

00:12:20.840 --> 00:12:22.220
Nice to meet you.

00:12:22.220 --> 00:12:24.380
Oh, that's Nacchan.

00:12:24.380 --> 00:12:26.140
I dressed her up.

00:12:26.140 --> 00:12:28.350
Dressed up! Nattsun is dressed up!

00:12:28.680 --> 00:12:30.810
That outfit looks great on you.

00:12:30.810 --> 00:12:33.560
Amazing! Nattsun turned cute!

00:12:33.560 --> 00:12:36.860
Y-You think so? That's kinda embarrassing...

00:12:36.860 --> 00:12:39.270
I know! I'm gonna take your picture!

00:12:39.270 --> 00:12:41.650
Huh?! I don't think a picture is...

00:12:41.650 --> 00:12:43.280
Oh, yeah, pictures.

00:12:43.280 --> 00:12:46.070
It'll probably be more fun 
if we make this image last.

00:12:46.740 --> 00:12:47.530
Okay, here goes.

00:12:47.530 --> 00:12:49.620
Whoa, you're actually taking one?

00:12:49.620 --> 00:12:50.540
Of course.

00:12:50.830 --> 00:12:52.410
Okay, Natsumi, here we go.

00:12:52.410 --> 00:12:54.370
That's great! You look cute!

00:12:54.370 --> 00:12:56.040
You really do look beautiful.

00:12:56.040 --> 00:12:57.540
Whoa, hang on...

00:12:57.880 --> 00:12:59.920
Come on, hurry up.

00:12:59.920 --> 00:13:02.760
Make a cute pose, too.

00:13:16.770 --> 00:13:19.900
Okay! Bring on the picture!

00:13:19.900 --> 00:13:23.230
There's no point in taking 
a picture of you like that.

00:13:23.230 --> 00:13:26.110
I guess even getting all that 
praise didn't help her.

00:13:29.450 --> 00:13:31.450
Hika-nee, I brought a snack.

00:13:31.450 --> 00:13:33.700
Oh, thanks.

00:13:33.700 --> 00:13:35.910
I was surprised when you just showed up.

00:13:36.250 --> 00:13:39.000
I didn't have anything else 
to do after visiting graves.

00:13:40.040 --> 00:13:41.750
So how's life in Tokyo?

00:13:41.750 --> 00:13:44.760
What's this? You wanna hear about Tokyo?

00:13:44.760 --> 00:13:45.760
No, not really.

00:13:45.760 --> 00:13:48.340
Oh, they're dumplings. 
Where'd these come from?

00:13:48.340 --> 00:13:50.350
They were in the fridge.

00:13:53.100 --> 00:13:55.890
Wow, is this red bean paste inside them?

00:13:55.890 --> 00:13:57.940
These go great with green tea.

00:14:01.650 --> 00:14:04.940
So anyway, I went to Yokohama a while ago.

00:14:04.940 --> 00:14:07.740
Yeah? What's Yokohama like?

00:14:07.740 --> 00:14:10.910
It's got the ocean, 
and buildings, and lots of people.

00:14:10.910 --> 00:14:12.910
Tokyo really is amazing.

00:14:15.370 --> 00:14:19.080
Whew, there were so many 
dumplings, and we ate them all.

00:14:19.500 --> 00:14:21.130
So what should we do?

00:14:21.130 --> 00:14:22.460
There you are.

00:14:22.960 --> 00:14:24.630
Oh, Renge's here, too?

00:14:24.630 --> 00:14:26.710
What brings you all here?

00:14:26.710 --> 00:14:31.720
We decided to go moon-viewing 
together after dinner.

00:14:31.720 --> 00:14:32.430
Yeah?

00:14:32.430 --> 00:14:33.970
It's that time of year already?

00:14:34.260 --> 00:14:39.440
So I came to tell you not 
to fill up on snacks.

00:14:39.690 --> 00:14:41.060
We have dumplings for later.

00:14:41.060 --> 00:14:42.230
Dumplings?!

00:14:42.230 --> 00:14:45.820
Don't you two eat the dumplings 
in the fridge, okay?

00:14:42.650 --> 00:14:45.820
I want dumplings! Dumplings!

00:14:45.820 --> 00:14:48.440
Okay, got it. We won't.

00:14:48.440 --> 00:14:51.030
We'll resist the sweets 
and get good and hungry.

00:14:51.320 --> 00:14:52.700
Okay, later, then.

00:14:54.200 --> 00:14:55.700
Dumplings!

00:14:55.700 --> 00:14:57.200
I get it already, Renge.

00:14:59.620 --> 00:15:02.790
We ate them. We ate the dumplings.

00:15:03.130 --> 00:15:05.300
We ate all of them with hot green tea.

00:15:05.300 --> 00:15:06.630
We're in trouble.

00:15:06.630 --> 00:15:08.800
Everyone was looking forward to those.

00:15:08.800 --> 00:15:11.050
Ren-chon was especially hyped up.

00:15:13.090 --> 00:15:15.310
What are we gonna do, Natsumi?!

00:15:15.310 --> 00:15:17.470
You should've told me they were 
moon-viewing dumplings, you idiot!

00:15:17.470 --> 00:15:19.730
Whoever calls someone is 
an idiot is an idiot!

00:15:19.730 --> 00:15:21.310
I can't help it if I didn't know!

00:15:21.310 --> 00:15:22.650
Okay, you egghead, then!

00:15:22.650 --> 00:15:25.400
Don't make fun of eggs! They're delicious!

00:15:29.240 --> 00:15:32.910
O-Okay, this isn't the time 
for us to be fighting.

00:15:32.910 --> 00:15:34.820
I just realized something.

00:15:34.820 --> 00:15:36.580
What? Do you have an idea?

00:15:36.580 --> 00:15:40.410
It's true that I didn't check to see if
they were moon-viewing dumplings.

00:15:40.410 --> 00:15:42.500
I apologize for that. Sorry.

00:15:43.630 --> 00:15:44.540
But...

00:15:45.000 --> 00:15:47.710
I didn't check to see if they 
were dumplings, either.

00:15:47.710 --> 00:15:48.760
Wh—

00:15:49.630 --> 00:15:50.840
What do you mean?

00:15:50.840 --> 00:15:55.890
I opened it without even looking 
at the name on the package.

00:15:57.810 --> 00:16:00.600
Yes. Those might have been

00:16:00.600 --> 00:16:04.100
sweet potatoes that tasted 
a lot like dumplings.

00:16:04.100 --> 00:16:07.150
As if! Listening to you was a waste of time!

00:16:07.150 --> 00:16:10.990
On what planet are there sweet potatoes 
stuffed with red bean jam, you moron?!

00:16:10.990 --> 00:16:13.490
Whoever calls someone a moron is a moron!

00:16:13.990 --> 00:16:15.660
Sitting around confused won't help.

00:16:15.660 --> 00:16:16.990
You pound some rice.

00:16:16.990 --> 00:16:18.080
We're making more?

00:16:18.080 --> 00:16:19.830
Can you make dumplings from rice?

00:16:19.830 --> 00:16:21.620
What are you gonna do, then?

00:16:21.620 --> 00:16:26.750
In case they find out you messed 
up and we ate the dumplings,

00:16:26.750 --> 00:16:28.420
I'm gonna go kill their good moods.

00:16:28.420 --> 00:16:30.710
Huh? What are you saying, Hika-nee?

00:16:30.710 --> 00:16:31.670
Are you okay?

00:16:31.670 --> 00:16:34.470
I don't want to hear that from the 
girl who brought up sweet potatoes!

00:16:34.880 --> 00:16:37.470
They'll get less mad if we 
bring down the mood slowly,

00:16:37.470 --> 00:16:40.600
than if they go from max excitement 
to rock bottom all at once, right?

00:16:40.720 --> 00:16:45.140
Don't you know how to parachute anger by
feeding depressing info in small amounts?!

00:16:45.440 --> 00:16:47.690
I-I see. So that's what you meant.

00:16:49.070 --> 00:16:51.280
Hey. Everyone having fun?

00:16:51.280 --> 00:16:52.570
Oh, Hikage-san.

00:16:52.570 --> 00:16:53.700
Welcome.

00:16:53.700 --> 00:16:55.410
Think you can stay over tonight?

00:16:55.410 --> 00:16:56.110
Huh?

00:16:56.110 --> 00:17:00.450
See, we're all gonna spend 
the night here tonight!

00:17:00.450 --> 00:17:03.080
We get to eat dumplings 
and play until nighttime!

00:17:03.080 --> 00:17:04.620
R-Really?

00:17:04.790 --> 00:17:08.130
Actually, you think the 
weather's gonna be okay?

00:17:08.130 --> 00:17:10.880
It might get cloudy.

00:17:10.880 --> 00:17:12.630
Maybe we shouldn't get too excited.

00:17:12.630 --> 00:17:13.920
It'll be fine.

00:17:13.920 --> 00:17:17.800
The forecast said today would be 
perfect moon-viewing weather.

00:17:17.800 --> 00:17:19.680
R-Really?

00:17:19.680 --> 00:17:22.890
But are you guys a little too psyched up?

00:17:22.890 --> 00:17:25.810
We're just looking at the moon. 
It's not that interesting....

00:17:25.810 --> 00:17:29.190
It'll be my first time eating 
dumplings while moon-viewing.

00:17:29.190 --> 00:17:34.150
Well, the dumplings might 
not taste that good...

00:17:34.610 --> 00:17:38.200
That reminds me. You're not 
putting anything in that vase?

00:17:38.200 --> 00:17:40.410
Oh, I forgot.

00:17:40.410 --> 00:17:43.450
I was going to pick some silver 
grass from somewhere...

00:17:43.700 --> 00:17:46.710
Why do people decorate with silver 
grass at moon-viewing time?

00:17:46.710 --> 00:17:49.170
No idea. Do you know, Hika-nee?

00:17:49.170 --> 00:17:54.050
Huh? Didn't people decorate with rice 
plants to celebrate a good harvest?

00:17:54.050 --> 00:17:57.630
They just used silver grass when 
they couldn't get rice plants.

00:17:57.630 --> 00:18:00.430
Oh, so it wasn't originally silver grass?

00:18:00.430 --> 00:18:02.810
We have rice plants up at my house.

00:18:02.810 --> 00:18:07.060
Oh, then maybe Kazuho-san would 
give us some if we asked?

00:18:07.060 --> 00:18:08.810
Hey, good idea!

00:18:08.810 --> 00:18:11.060
Let's go get some now!

00:18:11.060 --> 00:18:12.900
H-Hey, wait...

00:18:12.900 --> 00:18:16.030
If we're spending the night, 
I'll go get my pajamas.

00:18:16.030 --> 00:18:17.820
Oh, you can borrow mine.

00:18:17.820 --> 00:18:20.700
You love lending people clothes, 
don't you, Konomi-chan?

00:18:21.820 --> 00:18:23.700
<i>I just got them more excited.</i>

00:18:24.450 --> 00:18:26.000
Natsumi, how's it going on your end?

00:18:26.000 --> 00:18:28.210
It just turned into paste.

00:18:28.210 --> 00:18:29.170
You, too, huh?

00:18:29.170 --> 00:18:31.040
You mean you messed up, too?

00:18:31.040 --> 00:18:32.710
Yeah. I blew it.

00:18:32.710 --> 00:18:34.630
Hika-nee, should we apologize?

00:18:34.630 --> 00:18:36.210
I don't think we can do this!

00:18:36.210 --> 00:18:37.920
Y-Yeah...

00:18:37.920 --> 00:18:40.300
We can't change the fact that we ate them.

00:18:41.430 --> 00:18:42.680
Let's apologize.

00:18:43.550 --> 00:18:46.720
The one we really don't 
want mad at us is Konomi.

00:18:46.720 --> 00:18:48.730
Let's focus our kneeling toward Konomi.

00:18:48.730 --> 00:18:51.270
Huh?! I didn't say anything about kneeling!

00:18:51.270 --> 00:18:54.820
Well, Konomi should forgive us 
if we kneel down to apologize.

00:18:54.820 --> 00:18:56.280
Where is she now?

00:18:56.280 --> 00:18:58.650
They're all at my house.

00:18:58.650 --> 00:19:02.280
They'll be back soon, so let's wait 
by the door on our hands and knees.

00:19:02.280 --> 00:19:05.790
But that would mean kneeling 
in front of Ren-chon, too.

00:19:05.790 --> 00:19:06.830
Is that okay?

00:19:06.830 --> 00:19:08.370
No need for compassion.

00:19:09.290 --> 00:19:13.080
Even if she's my sister, when there's 
a need to apologize, I'll kneel.

00:19:13.080 --> 00:19:14.340
Wow, that's pathetic.

00:19:14.340 --> 00:19:16.960
We'll both apologize as 
soon as the door opens.

00:19:18.420 --> 00:19:21.630
I wasn't planning to do this 
on my hands and knees...

00:19:19.220 --> 00:19:23.300
So We're gonna look at the moon 
and eat dumplings after dinner!

00:19:23.550 --> 00:19:26.100
Eating dumplings while 
looking at the moon...

00:19:26.100 --> 00:19:28.560
People from old days sure 
knew what they were doing.

00:19:29.060 --> 00:19:30.940
Oh, you've got dumplings, too?

00:19:30.940 --> 00:19:33.520
<i>They brought someone kneeling won't work on!</i>

00:19:33.730 --> 00:19:36.020
Huh? What are you guys doing?

00:19:36.020 --> 00:19:38.530
Uh, w-well, this is...

00:19:38.530 --> 00:19:40.740
Well... Actually...

00:19:40.740 --> 00:19:43.410
Turtles! We were impersonating turtles!

00:19:43.410 --> 00:19:43.990
Huh?!

00:19:43.990 --> 00:19:47.450
Okay, Hika-nee! Let's go 
bask in the sun in my room!

00:19:47.450 --> 00:19:48.910
O-Okay!

00:19:49.450 --> 00:19:50.750
I don't get it.

00:19:50.750 --> 00:19:53.710
Oh, Kazu-chan and Kaede-chan are here, too?

00:19:53.710 --> 00:19:56.130
Yeah, Ren-chon invited us.

00:19:56.130 --> 00:19:59.960
This is some rice we picked 
at home. Please take it.

00:19:59.960 --> 00:20:03.380
Oh, my! You didn't have to do that for us.

00:20:03.380 --> 00:20:05.970
Hey! Why'd you say that when 
we had the perfect timing?!

00:20:05.970 --> 00:20:08.560
Kneeling won't work on Candy Store!

00:20:08.560 --> 00:20:10.560
Also, I forgot about Mom!

00:20:10.560 --> 00:20:12.480
Be glad you didn't have to do that 
in front of your little sister!

00:20:12.480 --> 00:20:15.770
I ended up showing her my 
turtle impersonation instead!

00:20:16.560 --> 00:20:20.570
Wait, Kazu-nee said she 
brought rice, didn't she?

00:20:20.990 --> 00:20:22.700
Yeah, she did.

00:20:23.490 --> 00:20:26.240
I didn't clean up the rice 
I turned into paste.

00:20:29.660 --> 00:20:31.370
Nattsun! Hika-nee!

00:20:31.370 --> 00:20:33.410
What is it, Ren-chon?

00:20:33.410 --> 00:20:35.920
Over here! This is amazing!

00:20:38.380 --> 00:20:43.340
Candy Store and Konomi-nee are 
making gohei mochi for us!

00:20:43.340 --> 00:20:46.640
With this many people, 
there might not be enough dumplings.

00:20:46.640 --> 00:20:50.850
There was some crushed rice in the 
kitchen, so Kaede-chan had the idea.

00:20:50.850 --> 00:20:53.270
Plus we had the rice Senpai brought over.

00:20:53.480 --> 00:20:56.520
What? Really? We're saved!

00:20:56.520 --> 00:20:58.310
Saved? What do you mean?

00:20:58.310 --> 00:21:02.990
Well, actually, Hika-nee and I ate all 
the dumplings without knowing anything.

00:21:02.990 --> 00:21:05.740
But if there's gohei 
mochi, it's okay, right?

00:21:09.950 --> 00:21:13.160
Huh? It's okay, right?

00:21:23.880 --> 00:21:25.930
Wow!

00:21:28.840 --> 00:21:31.640
It looks bigger than usual.

00:21:32.010 --> 00:21:33.560
It sure is pretty.

00:21:33.560 --> 00:21:35.810
It really feels like a harvest moon.

00:21:40.560 --> 00:21:43.440
Candy Store, my mochi's all gone.

00:21:43.690 --> 00:21:45.400
Should we order some more?

00:21:45.400 --> 00:21:46.530
Sounds good.

00:21:46.530 --> 00:21:48.950
You heard her. Another order of gohei mochi.

00:21:48.950 --> 00:21:50.910
Five of them. Make it quick.

00:21:50.910 --> 00:21:52.290
With pleasure!

00:21:52.290 --> 00:21:54.660
Hang tight just a bit longer!

00:22:10.430 --> 00:22:16.350
<b>Non Non Biyori</b>

00:22:16.350 --> 00:22:21.520
<b>That's all for today</b>

00:23:41.060 --> 00:23:42.940
<i>Konomi-nee's shell!</i>

00:23:42.940 --> 00:23:44.520
<i>That's how it always is at first.</i>

00:23:46.610 --> 00:23:48.190
<i>I'm a monster.</i>

00:23:48.190 --> 00:23:50.490
<i>What?! That's the first I've heard that!</i>

00:23:50.490 --> 00:23:53.490
<b>Temporarily</b>

00:23:50.490 --> 00:23:53.490
<b>Closed</b>

00:23:50.490 --> 00:23:53.490
<b>Episode 10</b>

00:23:50.490 --> 00:23:53.490
<b>I Practiced Really Hard</b>

00:23:53.490 --> 00:23:57.100
<b>Non Non Biyori
Repeat</b>

00:23:53.490 --> 00:23:57.100
Photo: Mato

00:23:53.490 --> 00:23:57.100
Please Watch Again
